# contour_boss.cam — the 3D-wire boss rim at extent=0: the reserved semantic
# itself (DECISIONS.md "the 3D-wire Contour…" — extent 0 means "add no
# extrusion", so the pass rides the wire, a trim edge). CW winding in plan
# view (standing material), both comp modes in one golden.
#
# Hand-checked anchors (40mm square 30..70, T5 dia 10 so r = 5; wire corners
# alternate z = -1 and z = -3):
#   - engine comp normalizes the projection to CCW and offsets OUTWARD to the
#     square 25..75 whose corners round into r=5 fillet arcs. Both endpoints
#     of a corner's arc re-attach through the two segments meeting at that
#     corner (clamped to the corner itself), so each arc is constant-Z at its
#     corner's own z: the arc at (70,30,z=-3) runs (75,30)->(70,25) [or
#     reversed by travel direction] wholly at Z-3.000, extent 0 adding
#     nothing.
#   - each straight side interpolates linearly between its corners' Z — the
#     bottom side's midpoint (50,25) passes exactly Z-2.000.
#   - control comp emits the authored CW edge with Z words: X30 Y30 Z-1.000,
#     X30 Y70 Z-3.000, X70 Y70 Z-1.000, X70 Y30 Z-3.000, D register D5.
units mm
feed 800
plunge 300
rapid_z 5
clearance_z 25
spindle 3000

stock Box(w=100, l=100, h=20, x=0, y=0, z=0)

tool T5 Endmill(dia=10.0)

feature Crest ContourBoss(extent=0
    30 30 -1
    30 70 -3
    70 70 -1
    70 30 -3
)

run Clear(tool=T5, profile=Crest, stepover=4.0, stepdown=4.0)
run Side(tool=T5, surface=Crest)
run Side(tool=T5, surface=Crest, comp=control)
